{"availability":"available","full":"seto77/PDIndexer","name":"PDIndexer","description":"PDIndexer is a powder X-ray / neutron diffraction analysis tool: it displays diffraction profiles, overlays the calculated diffraction lines of known crystals, fits peaks to refine lattice constants, and estimates pressure from the equations of state of standard materials.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C#","stars":15,"forks":3,"created":"2019-12-20T07:21:58Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:23:44Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://seto77.github.io/PDIndexer/","topics":["cif","crystal-structure","crystallography","csharp","diamond-anvil-cell","equation-of-state","high-pressure","materials-science","mineral-physics","mineralogy","neutron-diffraction","peak-fitting","phase-identification","powder-diffraction","synchrotron","winforms","x-ray-diffraction","xrd-analysis"],"demo":"https://seto77.github.io/PDIndexer/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:51.042Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:51.042Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:51.042Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:51.042Z","stars":15,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["PDIndexer is a free and open-source GUI-based application for analyzing one-dimensional powder diffraction patterns from laboratory / synchrotron X-rays and neutron time-of-flight (TOF) measurements. It displays measured profiles, overlays the diffraction lines calculated from crystal structures, processes and calibrates profiles, fits peaks to refine lattice constants by least squares, and estimates pressure from the equations of state (EOS) of standard materials. PDIndexer assists a wide range of researchers working in high-pressure science, powder X-ray diffraction, and synchrotron/neutron…","PDIndexer has been continuously developed since 2005 and is distributed together with its sister application IPAnalyzer, which converts two-dimensional dete